  "body": "Found while working #44 (comment https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/44#issuecomment-6798765160) and #7 round 10.\n\n**What happens:** on main (4865500d, release, `HSM_ONE=island hsm_one`) the growth planner (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/grow.rs`) runs for about 68 s before the #13 budget (`adaptive/budget.rs`, 30,000 tool radii of summed revolution length) refuses the plan and the op falls back to Offset rings by name. The budget counts path length, not planner time: only 15-25 % of the time is the stock walk the counter follows; the rest is whole-ring polygon geometry on every trial step.\n\n**Expected:** a region the planner cannot finish is refused in seconds, not after a minute of silent work (\"plans in seconds or refuses\"; a hang-like wait on a user-triggered path is a Prime Directive matter).\n\n**Evidence** (from the #44 probe, branch `issue/44-incremental-ring-walk`, commit 1dc7b945, DO NOT MERGE - diagnostic only):\n- island, margin 1.0: ran out of margin after 34.2 s in grow (4.9 s of it the stock walk)\n- island, margin 1.6: refused by the budget after 163 revolutions, 34.0 s in grow\n- #845's held fix roughly doubles the growth work, so it makes this worse unless the bound lands first or with it.\n\n**Options:** a wall-time or trial-count bound beside the work budget; an earlier estimate that refuses before planning (the up-front estimate exists for long channels - extend it to islanded regions); or cheaper per-trial geometry. Whichever is taken, the fallback stays named and visible.\n\nDone means: a test pins that the island fixture (and the 14 mm band) either plans or is refused within a stated bound, the refusal names the reason, and no adaptive golden changes.\n\nRelated: #44, #7, #845, #13.\n",
